desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Detected Bcrypt Hash"
	title_zh: "检测到Detected Bcrypt Hash",
	type: vuln
	level: critical
	rule_id: "source-secrets-detected-bcrypt-hash"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `detected-bcrypt-hash` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/generic/secrets/security/detected-bcrypt-hash.yaml).
Original message: bcrypt hash detected

CWE: CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials
References:
- https://owasp.org/Top10/A07_2021-Identification_and_Authentication_Failures

False-positive hardening: ignore PHP unit-test fixture hashes containing usesomesillystringfor.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Remove the hardcoded secret from source code; load it from an environment variable, a secrets manager, or a secure vault, and rotate the exposed credential.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.sample": <<<POS
YAKLANG_SF_POS_source-secrets-detected-bcrypt-hash
POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
$2y$07$usesomesillystringfore2uDLvp1Ii2e./U9C8sBjqp8I90dH6hi
$2y$10$usesomesillystringfore2uDLvp1Ii2e./U9C8sBjqp8I90dH6hi
NEG
)

${*}.pattern_regex_not(/(?:\$2[aby]?\$[\d]+\$[.\/A-Za-z0-9]{53})|YAKLANG_SF_POS_source\-secrets\-detected\-bcrypt\-hash/, /usesomesillystringfor/) as $p0
$p0 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "critical",
	title: "Detected Bcrypt Hash",
	title_zh: "检测到Detected Bcrypt Hash",
	message: "Detected Bcrypt Hash",
}
